.\" man/man3/Docv::Viewer::Picker.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Viewer::Picker" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer::Picker \- A fuzzy\-filtered, ranked list with a selection: the page search, and the ranking behind finding in the page.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Viewer::Picker\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A fuzzy\-filtered, ranked list with a selection: the page search, and
the ranking behind finding in the page.
.PP
The query splits into space\-separated terms, each a \fB\%Fuzzy\fR matcher.
Every term must match an item\(aqs label, or its detail when details are
searched. A term counts with the better of its label score plus
\fB\%LABEL_BONUS\fR and its detail score. Items of a lower group come first
(the project\(aqs pages and documents in the page search); within a
group the best score wins, and ties go to the shorter label, then to
the item order. An empty query lists every item in order.
.PP
A \fInested\fR picker shows its items as an \fB\%Outline\fR: groups of items
sharing a name prefix, folded until opened. An empty query lists the
outline in its order; a query ranks each level by the best match
under it, leaves out groups without matches and opens the others
until they are folded by hand.
.PP
Rows scroll sideways (\fB\%scroll_x\fR) when they are wider than the view,
and items can carry hit counts (\fB\%hits=\fR), drawn at the right edge of
their rows in \fB\%Hit\fR.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBFOLDED = \(aq\[u25B8]\(aq\fR
Marks of a folded and an open group, and the columns they take.
.PP
\fBGROUP_DETAIL = "pages"\fR
.TP 4
\fBGROUP_ROLE = Theme::Role::Name\fR
The role of group labels and the word after a group\(aqs item count.
.TP 4
\fBLABEL_BONUS = Fuzzy::SCORE_MATCH // 2\fR
What a label match is worth above an equal detail match.
.TP 4
\fBLABEL_PERCENT = 40\fR
Widest label column in percent of the width; details follow in a
column, or two columns after a longer label.
.PP
\fBMARKER_WIDTH = 2\fR
.PP
\fBOPEN = \(aq\[u25BE]\(aq\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(items : Array(Item), search_details : Bool = true, nested : Bool = false)\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef collapse(rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Folds the selected group, or moves to the group around the selected
row when it is folded or an item.
.TP 4
\fBdef current : Item | Nil\fR
The selected item; \fB\%nil\fR on a group.
.TP 4
\fBdef draw(screen : Screen, row : Int32, col : Int32, rows : Int32, cols : Int32, styles : Array(UInt16), hover : Int32 | Nil = nil, fill : UInt16 = 0_u16, details : Bool = true) : Nil\fR
Draws \fIrows\fR rows into \fIcols\fR columns of \fIscreen\fR from (\fIrow\fR,
\fIcol\fR) with the role style ids \fIstyles\fR (\fB\%Theme#styles\fR), scrolled
sideways by \fB\%left\fR: labels in their item\(aqs role (groups in
\fB\%GROUP_ROLE\fR, after their mark), with \fIdetails\fR their details in
\fB\%Detail\fR, the selected row on \fB\%Selection\fR, the visible row \fIhover\fR
under the pointer on \fB\%Hover\fR and matched characters in \fB\%Mark\fR, all
over \fIfill\fR. Rows with hits take \fB\%Hit\fR on their labels and show the
count at the right edge.
.TP 4
\fBdef expand(rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Opens the selected group, or moves into it when it is open.
.TP 4
\fBdef group? : Bool\fR
True when the selected row is a group.
.TP 4
\fBdef hits : Array(Int32) | Nil\fR
Hit counts per item (\fB\%hits=\fR), if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef hits=(counts : Array(Int32) | Nil) : Array(Int32) | Nil\fR
Sets the hit counts per item (\fB\%Corpus#count\fR); an outline\(aqs groups
count their items with hits. \fB\%nil\fR removes them.
.PP
\fBdef items : Array(Item)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef items=(items : Array(Item)) : Array(Item)\fR
Replaces the items, keeping the query, the open groups while the
keys stay the same, and the selected row when the selection was
moved.
.TP 4
\fBdef label_width : Int32\fR
Columns the widest label takes, with its indentation and mark.
.TP 4
\fBdef left : Int32\fR
Columns the rows are scrolled sideways.
.TP 4
\fBdef marks(index : Int32) : Tuple(Array(Int32), Array(Int32))\fR
Matched character positions in the label and the detail of item
\fIindex\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef max_top(rows : Int32) : Int32\fR
The largest \fB\%top\fR for a view of \fIrows\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef move(delta : Int32, rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Moves the selection by \fIdelta\fR and scrolls it into a view of \fIrows\fR.
.PP
\fBdef outline : Outline | Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef query : String\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef query=(text : String) : String\fR
Sets the query and selects the best match.
.TP 4
\fBdef results : Array(Int32)\fR
Indices into \fB\%items\fR of the matching items, best first.
.TP 4
\fBdef reveal(target : Int32, rows : Int32) : Bool\fR
Selects the item with \fItarget\fR, unfolding the groups around it, and
scrolls it into a view of \fIrows\fR; false when no item has it.
.TP 4
\fBdef rows : Array(Int32)\fR
The rows shown: node ids of the \fB\%outline\fR when nested, otherwise
\fB\%results\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef scroll_to(top : Int32, rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Scrolls a view of \fIrows\fR to \fItop\fR, keeping the selection in view.
.TP 4
\fBdef scroll_x(delta : Int32, cols : Int32, details : Bool) : Nil\fR
Scrolls sideways by \fIdelta\fR columns in a view of \fIcols\fR columns
(\fB\%draw\fR\(aqs), with or without \fIdetails\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef select_row(row : Int32) : Bool\fR
Selects visible \fIrow\fR; false when the row is empty.
.TP 4
\fBdef selected : Int32\fR
Index into \fB\%rows\fR of the selected row.
.TP 4
\fBdef toggle(rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Opens or folds the selected group in a view of \fIrows\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef top : Int32\fR
Index into \fB\%rows\fR of the first visible row.
.TP 4
\fBdef unfold(rows : Int32) : Nil\fR
Opens folded groups level by level, in outline order, while the rows
still fit in \fIrows\fR; a group whose items would not fit stays folded.
Only without a query.
.TP 4
\fBdef width(details : Bool) : Int32\fR
Columns of the widest row: its label, and with \fIdetails\fR its detail
after the label column.
